==Latin==
[[Image:France map with Loire highlighted.jpg|thumb|350px|''<b>Tabula</b> Franciae cum flumine Ligere insignata''<sup> {{w|Liger|lang=la|W}}</sup><br><u>Map</u> of France with river Loire]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{link|la|tabla|||tr=|pos=|g=|id=}} {{qualifier|Vulgar or Late Latin, Appendix Probi}}

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unk|la|title=uncertain}}. 
* Some connect it with {{m|la|taberna}};
* Some refer it to {{der|la|ine-pro|*tal-dʰleh₂}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*telh₂-|t=flat}};
* Some refer it to {{der|la|ine-pro|*th₂-dʰleh₂}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*teh₂-|t=to stand}} (a variety of {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-}} without [[s-mobile]], whence also Latin {{m|la|sto|stō, stāre|t=to stand}}) + {{m|ine-pro|*-dʰlom|pos=instrumental suffix}} whence Latin {{m|la|-bula}}. The original meaning would then be “that which stands”, for which see also Latin {{m|la|stabulum}}.

